Q: What are the other diagnostic tests or examinations for hemorrhoids?
A: Internal hemorrhoids can be viewed only using the anoscope or the flexible sigmoidoscope. Hemorrhoids appear as bulging bluish masses above the dentate line. If there are accompanying constitutional symptoms (e.g. weight loss), colonoscopy should be done to exclude colon cancer.
